  <h1>AI-Powered Incident Triage Assistant</h1>
  <p style="font-size: 13pt; color: #475569; font-weight: bold;">
    Enterprise Architecture Specification & Use Case Document
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Executive Summary:</strong> The AI-Powered Incident Triage Assistant is an autonomous site reliability engineering system designed to ingest unstructured incident logs, classify severity (P0–P3) and technical failure domains, retrieve relevant runbooks via hybrid semantic RAG, and route tickets to responsible on-call engineering teams with sub-millisecond latency.
  </div>

  <h2>1. Problem Statement & Business Justification</h2>
  <p>
    During critical production outages, Site Reliability Engineers (SREs) and DevOps teams face severe challenges that directly impact company revenue, customer trust, and service availability:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Alert Fatigue:</strong> Production monitoring tools (Datadog, Sentry, CloudWatch) emit hundreds of unprioritized alerts daily, making it difficult to isolate root causes.</li>
    <li><strong>High Mean Time to Acknowledge (MTTA):</strong> Engineers spend an average of 15–45 minutes manually triaging tickets, deciphering stack traces, and searching knowledge bases.</li>
    <li><strong>Misrouted Incidents:</strong> Incidents are frequently misdirected across team silos (e.g., database connection pool exhaustion incorrectly assigned to the frontend web team), creating response delays.</li>
    <li><strong>Underutilized Historical Knowledge:</strong> Detailed post-mortems and Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) often sit idle in wikis rather than being surfaced automatically during active outages.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Quantitative Performance Metrics (Benchmark Evaluation)</h2>
  <p>
    The system was evaluated against 18 ground-truth labeled synthetic incidents covering realistic multi-service failures across the entire software stack:
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 14pt;">
    <div class="kpi-box">
      <span class="kpi-number">100%</span>
      <span class="kpi-label">Severity Accuracy</span>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-box">
      <span class="kpi-number">100%</span>
      <span class="kpi-label">Category Isolation</span>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-box">
      <span class="kpi-number">100%</span>
      <span class="kpi-label">Team Routing</span>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-box">
      <span class="kpi-number">0.3 ms</span>
      <span class="kpi-label">Average Latency</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>3. End-to-End System Architecture</h2>
  <p>The solution comprises five decoupled architectural layers:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Ingestion Layer:</strong> Ingests ticket descriptions, raw stack traces, error codes, and telemetry from users or simulated streams.</li>
    <li><strong>RAG Knowledge Base:</strong> 15 multi-domain SRE runbooks indexed via an inverted index with BM25 term weighting and symptom signature boosting.</li>
    <li><strong>Dual-Engine Triage Orchestrator:</strong>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Local Deterministic RAG (Default):</strong> High-speed semantic engine that runs 100% offline with zero external API key requirements.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Gemini 2.5 Flash:</strong> Advanced multi-modal reasoning engine leveraging the official <code>@google/genai</code> SDK for dynamic post-mortem synthesis.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Escalation & Action Matrix:</strong> Determines blast radius, computes SLA response times, assigns on-call leads, and generates one-click copyable diagnostic commands.</li>
    <li><strong>User Interface & Presentation:</strong> Modern web dashboard providing a Live Triage Console, Synthetic Incident Feed, Runbook Knowledge Explorer, and Benchmark View.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>4. Multi-Domain Knowledge Base Catalog</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Domain / Category</th>
        <th>Runbook ID</th>
        <th>Scenario Title</th>
        <th>Assigned Escalation Team</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Database</strong></td>
        <td>RB-DB-001</td>
        <td>PostgreSQL Connection Pool Exhaustion</td>
        <td>Data & Database Platform</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Database</strong></td>
        <td>RB-DB-002</td>
        <td>PostgreSQL Deadlocks and Blocked Transactions</td>
        <td>Data & Database Platform</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Security & Auth</strong></td>
        <td>RB-SEC-001</td>
        <td>OAuth2 / JWT Signature Verification & JWKS Key Rotation</td>
        <td>Security Operations (SecOps)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Security & Auth</strong></td>
        <td>RB-SEC-002</td>
        <td>Credential Stuffing & Distributed Brute-Force Attack</td>
        <td>Security Operations (SecOps)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Security & Auth</strong></td>
        <td>RB-SEC-003</td>
        <td>TLS/mTLS Certificate Expiration & Auto-Renewal Failure</td>
        <td>Security Operations (SecOps)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Infrastructure</strong></td>
        <td>RB-INFRA-001</td>
        <td>Kubernetes Pod OOMKilled (Exit Code 137) CrashLoop</td>
        <td>SRE & Infrastructure</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Infrastructure</strong></td>
        <td>RB-INFRA-002</td>
        <td>Persistent Volume Claim (PVC) Disk Space Exhaustion (>95%)</td>
        <td>SRE & Infrastructure</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>API & Microservices</strong></td>
        <td>RB-API-001</td>
        <td>Gateway 504 Timeout & Cascading Circuit Breaker Trips</td>
        <td>Core API & Microservices</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>API & Microservices</strong></td>
        <td>RB-API-002</td>
        <td>Redis Cache Stampede and Connection Saturation</td>
        <td>Core API & Microservices</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>API & Microservices</strong></td>
        <td>RB-API-003</td>
        <td>Deprecated API Endpoint Sunset & Migration Enforcement</td>
        <td>Core API & Microservices</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Billing & Payments</strong></td>
        <td>RB-PAY-001</td>
        <td>Payment Webhook Failure and Signature Mismatch (Stripe)</td>
        <td>Payments & Monetization</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Billing & Payments</strong></td>
        <td>RB-PAY-002</td>
        <td>Payment Idempotency Key Conflicts & Double-Click Collisions</td>
        <td>Payments & Monetization</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Frontend & Client</strong></td>
        <td>RB-FE-001</td>
        <td>Single Page App Webpack/Vite ChunkLoadError Post-Deployment</td>
        <td>Frontend Platform</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Network & CDN</strong></td>
        <td>RB-NET-001</td>
        <td>Cluster-Wide CoreDNS Resolution Failures & Timeouts</td>
        <td>SRE & Infrastructure</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Network & CDN</strong></td>
        <td>RB-NET-002</td>
        <td>Edge CDN Ingress Transit Latency & POP Degradation</td>
        <td>SRE & Infrastructure</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
